  "summary": "Jodit Editor vulnerable to cross-site scripting",
  "details": "Cross-site scripting in the Jodit Editor rich text component: an `<iframe>` whose `src` used the `javascript:` scheme (for example `<iframe src=\"JavaScript: alert(/xss/)\">`) kept its `src` after sanitisation. Reported against 4.0.0-beta.86; the attribute survived up to 4.10.3. The sanitiser rewrite in jodit 4.11.2 strips such `src` values entirely, and the exact payload is pinned in the regression suite (xdan/jodit#1017).",
